{"description":"GitHub issue maleolabs/eka-cli#25 (suggestion, low, source: agent, EKA 1.2.0): authoring an 18-object planning package cost 36 sequential MCP round trips; reporter claims no batch surface and no MCP draft mutation, forcing hand-editing of workspace files.\n\nVerified against source - claim is PARTIALLY valid:\n- REFUTED in part: batch publishing EXISTS at CLI level (eka publish --all/--pending, topological order, cmd/authoring_batch.go) and eka new --file \u003cbatch.json\u003e scaffolds a related draft set in one call. What is missing is MCP exposure of these modes (MCP publish accepts exactly one target).\n- CONFIRMED: no MCP tool mutates an existing draft after scaffolding (tool inventory: get, domain, status, context, validate, new, publish, transition, note, view, draft_list, integrity_check, discard). eka edit is TTY-only and refuses non-TTY with guidance toward --content-file.\n- CONFIRMED design inconsistency: skills documentation explicitly instructs agents to edit draft files directly at known filesystem paths (\u003cworkspace\u003e/drafts/\u003cproject\u003e/\u003ctype\u003e-\u003cid\u003e.json), contradicting the 'never touch workspace storage by hand' boundary - while the MCP new report deliberately NEVER reveals the draft path, so an MCP-only agent is told to bypass a boundary it cannot even locate.\n\nFix direction: (1) MCP draft_update tool (target + partial content merge) to close the sanctioned-boundary hole - highest value; (2) expose batch mode on MCP publish at parity with CLI; (3) DECLINE scaffold+publish single-call merging - it conflates two lifecycle steps and weakens the draft gate.","acceptanceCriteria":"- New MCP tool draft_update (target + partial content merge) mutates a pending draft strictly inside the sanctioned API surface; publish still validates the final artifact (mutation does not bypass CKO gates).\n- MCP publish tool exposes batch mode (--pending/--all parity with CLI topological batch publish).\n- Skills documentation (eka-knowledge-authoring, eka-troubleshooting, installation docs) updated to reference draft_update instead of instructing direct draft-file edits.\n- Reporter's option 3 (merge scaffold+publish into one call) formally declined with rationale recorded in the closing comment: it collapses two lifecycle steps and weakens the draft review gate that immutable/gated authoring depends on.\n- Tests cover draft_update merge semantics (partial overwrite, unknown target refusal, post-publish refusal) and batch publish ordering.\n- Review findings posted as a comment on maleolabs/eka-cli#25; issue closed only after the fix ships in a release."}